{
  "slug": "tally-sync-running-vs-completed",
  "title": "How to Tell a Running Sync From a Completed One",
  "description": "Read the connector status before checking a change in the dashboard or pressing Sync Now again.",
  "category": "Sync troubleshooting",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Let the current run finish",
      "body": "When the connector shows that a sync is in progress, wait for the final result. Write down the start time if the run is taking longer than expected. Pressing the sync button again does not make an in-progress operation proof of success."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Read the result for the intended company",
      "body": "When the run ends, check whether it succeeded for the company you are working with. A recent clock time alone does not establish that the intended company synced. Record the reported result and any error text."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Verify one expected update",
      "body": "Open the dashboard and check a voucher that should have appeared after the run. Compare type, number and amount with TallyPrime. If it remains absent and the correct filters are already set, share the completed run time and reference with support."
    }
  ],
  "relatedPaths": [
    "/guides/tally-sync-troubleshooting",
    "/support"
  ]
}
